 "violations": [
  "Notice About Water Monitoring Violation (PDF page 5, Tier 3 notice on behalf of the SFRWS): due to an equipment failure, SFPUC monitoring of recycled filter backwash water turbidity at the Sunol Valley Water Treatment Plant was not conducted from June 23 to July 2, 2025; monitoring at other points showed treated water met all drinking water standards; the instrument was repaired and returned to service July 3, 2025; not an emergency, no action required.",
  "Report states that in 2025 tap water met all state and federal drinking water health standards; no MCL or AL exceedances; lead/copper 0 of 51 tap samples above the AL."
 ],
 "extraction_notes": "All table rows are on PDF page 4 (a two-page spread printed as report pages 4–5). Source columns: 'Groundwater Well', 'Valley Water', 'SFPUC'; each column prints 'Average or [Max]' and 'Range'. Distribution-system rows (lead/copper, disinfectant residual, TTHM, HAA5) have no source column -> source_group null. Cells printed 'NA' (pH and Temperature for SFPUC) and blank cells (Groundwater for TOC, Giardia, TT turbidity) produced no entry. Where the average is printed 'ND' but the range shows a detection (e.g. 'ND–0.12'), the entry is detected=true with value=range_high and average=null. Ranges printed 'ND–x' use range_low 0. Three turbidity (TT) sub-rows: Valley Water [0.5]/100%, SFPUC filtered [0.3]/100%, SFPUC unfiltered Hetch Hetchy [3.4]/0.3–0.5; '100%' is a compliance percentage, stored in notes, not as a range. Chlorate unit printed 'ppm' is almost certainly a misprint for ppb (NL 800; see notes). Temperature printed in ºF. mcl_printed for 'Other water quality parameters' rows holds the NL column ('800' or 'NS'); for lead/copper the AL printed in parentheses '(15)'/'(1.3)'; MRDL/MRDLG printed '[4]'. Hexavalent chromium footnote: compliance monitoring begins 2026-10-01. Radiological footnote: Valley Water gross alpha/uranium detected in San Luis Reservoir in 2022 (sample_year 2022); ND radiological cells have sample_year null (nine-year cycle, year not stated). All other rows default to sample_year 2025, although the report notes some data were collected before 2025 under reduced monitoring. PFAS/UCMR5/lithium entries (page 6) come from the narrative 'no chemicals, including regulated PFAS, were detected' and are not table rows; they are flagged in notes. Report says 21 parameters were detected; only detected parameters are listed in the table."
}